      "topic": "Latch and journal",
      "conclusion": "State latched before serialization/IO; first/all events and interrupted original exceptions retained; journal FD exclusive and kept open, full writes/fsync; missing or dirty journal terminal at supervisor. Not immutable against hostile in-process code or native syscalls."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Checkpoints",
      "conclusion": "Pre/post evaluation encloses float conversion and exception paths. Source checkpoint after imports occurs before temporal helper/dict/waveform; finally after native counter ensures denial inside waveform aborts returned value. Cannot interrupt already running C; auxiliary LAL calls are not the waveform counter."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Finalization",
      "conclusion": "AuditViolation overrides budget/partial status; checkpoint before diagnostics/result and after result. A late denied event after receipt invalidates external journal/returncode; no successful continuation solely from stale status."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Supervisor",
      "conclusion": "Validates identity, process return, audit states/journal pin/checkpoint counts, initialization consistency and failure counters; rejects missing/malformed receipts and stops next job; campaign incomplete/nonaccepted returns2."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Limits",
      "conclusion": "Scientific resource/sampler/source calls and declared limits preserved. Inherited3610s initial child wait plus unbounded post-kill wait/IO remains explicitly OPEN, not a new hard wall guarantee."
    },
    {
      "topic": "21 doubles",
      "conclusion": "Nine latch/checkpoint/exception tests, ten result-acceptance tests and two campaign-flow tests are logically aligned with intended defect. Source/native and supervisor process integration are modeled doubles, not invoked. PreopenedJournal actual short-write/fsync and real sys.addaudithook integration are not dynamically exercised; no execution claimed."
    }
